ng\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Remove the toothed pulley from the crankshaft housing.</p><p>2. Remove the fastening tab.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/244002432.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Place the fastening tab in position.</p><p>- Position the pulley in the special housing on the crankshaft.</p>"],[15,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/244000667\">Op. 1020D10 FRONT CRANK SHAFT OIL SEAL COVER - R + R AND REPLACE SEALS WITH TIMING BELT REMOVED</a></p><p>1. Make two millings on the toothed drive pulley (1a) and remove the pulley using a suitable extractor (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/244002433.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Place the toothed drive pulley in the oven.</p><p>1. Fit the drive pulley ensuring that the groove (1a) coincides with the key (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\